1225
00:42:58.000 --> 00:43:01.010
pushing heavy weights and working close to a 1RM.

1226
00:43:01.010 --> 00:43:03.450
Then week 13, an eight and a half

1227
00:43:03.450 --> 00:43:05.330
to a nine and half RPE single on squat and bench.

1228
00:43:05.330 --> 00:43:07.385
And deadlift at nine, nine and a half,

1229
00:43:07.385 --> 00:43:11.420
getting finally your three months into this retraining

1230
00:43:11.420 --> 00:43:14.220
which was the exact time the detraining was,

1231
00:43:14.220 --> 00:43:17.500
and can you get back to where you were in three months?

1232
00:43:17.500 --> 00:43:19.661
And I think if you use this strategy,

1233
00:43:19.661 --> 00:43:22.789
you can get some neuromuscular adaptations

1234
00:43:22.789 --> 00:43:25.150
and push those lifts up there towards

1235
00:43:25.150 --> 00:43:26.500
the end of this training block.

1236
00:43:26.500 --> 00:43:30.163
So, some thoughts and wisdom from doing this.

1237
00:43:31.000 --> 00:43:33.860
Typically I don't take a whole lot of time off

1238
00:43:33.860 --> 00:43:35.110
from training just to take it.

1239
00:43:35.110 --> 00:43:36.510
Although I've certainly had times

1240
00:43:36.510 --> 00:43:37.570
that have been busy in my life

1241
00:43:37.570 --> 00:43:38.463
and I've had to.

1242
00:43:39.857 --> 00:43:41.830
And you know we all have little injuries

1243
00:43:41.830 --> 00:43:43.078
and things and so forth

1244
00:43:43.078 --> 00:43:44.820
from time to time.

1245
00:43:44.820 --> 00:43:46.730
But I have had times where I've had to come back

1246
00:43:46.730 --> 00:43:48.500
from being off for a couple months or so.

1247
00:43:48.500 --> 00:43:50.680
So if you go through something like this,

1248
00:43:50.680 --> 00:43:52.870
just from being there, and I'm sure many many people

1249
00:43:52.870 --> 00:43:54.796
watching this video have been there as well,

1250
00:43:54.796 --> 00:43:58.310
just do something, it will cause progress.

1251
00:43:58.310 --> 00:44:00.130
You will progress quickly as well.

1252
00:44:00.130 --> 00:44:01.910
Right, if you can think back to when you first started

1253
00:44:01.910 --> 00:44:02.970
to train, years ago,

1254
00:44:02.970 --> 00:44:05.440
or maybe you're in the early stages of your training

1255
00:44:05.440 --> 00:44:07.240
career now, it's really fun, right?

1256
00:44:07.240 --> 00:44:09.304
You start to gain pretty quickly.

1257
00:44:09.304 --> 00:44:11.070
You're going to do that,

1258
00:44:11.070 --> 00:44:12.127
so enjoy it, right?

1259
00:44:12.127 --> 00:44:15.193
If you wanna do more, don't do it.

1260
00:44:16.130 --> 00:44:17.820
You know, stick to the plan,

1261
00:44:17.820 --> 00:44:19.880
if you get passed the first three months or so,

1262
00:44:19.880 --> 00:44:21.660
if you've been off for three months,

1263
00:44:21.660 --> 00:44:22.710
I think that's a pretty good rule,

1264
00:44:22.710 --> 00:44:24.660
as long as you've been off,

1265
00:44:24.660 --> 00:44:26.520
once you've started training for that amount

1266
00:44:26.520 --> 00:44:27.360
of time again

1267
00:44:27.360 --> 00:44:28.710
and then you start to wanna do more,

1268
00:44:28.710 --> 00:44:31.040
and push it or go off the plan, it's okay.

1269
00:44:31.040 --> 00:44:32.730
But if you're within those first three months

1270
00:44:32.730 --> 00:44:33.980
and you've got three months off,

1271
00:44:33.980 --> 00:44:36.560
don't do more than you're supposed to.

1272
00:44:36.560 --> 00:44:38.000
You're going to make progress

1273
00:44:38.000 --> 00:44:40.280
'cause you did nothing and now you do something.

1274
00:44:40.280 --> 00:44:41.710
So enjoy that.

1275
00:44:41.710 --> 00:44:43.150
Now once you get passed these three months

1276
00:44:43.150 --> 00:44:45.150
and you're making really fast progress,

1277
00:44:45.150 --> 00:44:47.410
you're not gonna expect the same progress

1278
00:44:47.410 --> 00:44:49.260
in the next block after this, right?

1279
00:44:49.260 --> 00:44:51.010
That's when you're probably gonna start to level off

1280
00:44:51.010 --> 00:44:51.843
a little bit.

1281
00:44:51.843 --> 00:44:53.140
So temper your expectations.

1282
00:44:53.140 --> 00:44:54.540
And if you're new to training,

1283
00:44:54.540 --> 00:44:56.384
you're probably making all this progress now,

1284
00:44:56.384 --> 00:44:58.340
but it's not gonna last forever, right?

1285
00:44:58.340 --> 00:44:59.740
So temper your expectations.

1286
00:45:00.900 --> 00:45:02.340
So applications and takeaways,

1287
00:45:02.340 --> 00:45:04.580
again, following months of detraining,

1288
00:45:04.580 --> 00:45:05.990
you will lose size and strength,

1289
00:45:05.990 --> 00:45:07.910
but it's probably not as much as you think,

1290
00:45:07.910 --> 00:45:09.470
when you start back, work gradually

1291
00:45:09.470 --> 00:45:11.710
and understand that your previous numbers

1292
00:45:11.710 --> 00:45:12.920
simply don't apply.

1293
00:45:12.920 --> 00:45:13.847
If you start back the first week

1294
00:45:13.847 --> 00:45:16.400
and say oh well I could squat 225 before,

1295
00:45:16.400 --> 00:45:19.555
and so you know I've done 175 for twelve,

1296
00:45:19.555 --> 00:45:22.238
so you know I'll just do 175 kilos

1297
00:45:22.238 --> 00:45:24.290
for a bunch of fives on my first day,

1298
00:45:24.290 --> 00:45:25.760
I should still be able to do that,

1299
00:45:25.760 --> 00:45:27.090
don't do it.

1300
00:45:27.090 --> 00:45:28.065
Could you do it?

1301
00:45:28.065 --> 00:45:30.130
Even that, that's probably a little much,

1302
00:45:30.130 --> 00:45:31.340
probably not,

1303
00:45:31.340 --> 00:45:33.130
but even if you could, don't do it.

1304
00:45:33.130 --> 00:45:35.030
Your previous numbers do not apply.

1305
00:45:35.030 --> 00:45:37.179
Program some absurdly light loads

1306
00:45:37.179 --> 00:45:39.730
and start back, don't do more than you need to.

1307
00:45:39.730 --> 00:45:41.070
And then just stay calm and focused.

1308
00:45:41.070 --> 00:45:41.903
Your adaptations will come back

1309
00:45:41.903 --> 00:45:43.510
and it won't take that long.

1310
00:45:43.510 --> 00:45:44.650
You know , I can't stress this enough,

1311
00:45:44.650 --> 00:45:45.660
if you do plan on training

1312
00:45:45.660 --> 00:45:47.060
for many many years,

1313
00:45:47.060 --> 00:45:48.913
and I'm sure a lot of us do,

1314
00:45:48.913 --> 00:45:51.480
then, it's gonna get there.

1315
00:45:51.480 --> 00:45:53.000
You just have to be patient with it.

1316
00:45:53.000 --> 00:45:55.730
It's not easy and I break that rule all the time myself,

1317
00:45:55.730 --> 00:45:58.430
so it's more of a "do as I say, not as I do"

1318
00:45:58.430 --> 00:46:00.170
type of thing, 'cause I'm not a very good coach

1319
00:46:00.170 --> 00:46:01.466
with myself.

1320
00:46:01.466 --> 00:46:04.152
But you know if you can stay patient,

1321
00:46:04.152 --> 00:46:05.740
stay calm and stay focused,

1322
00:46:05.740 --> 00:46:08.170
and trust that this gradual process will work,

1323
00:46:08.170 --> 00:46:09.300
it ultimately will work

1324
00:46:09.300 --> 00:46:10.730
and then there will be a time to push it

1325
00:46:10.730 --> 00:46:11.910
and go off plan later on.

1326
00:46:11.910 --> 00:46:14.800
But not in the first three months that you're coming back.

1327
00:46:14.800 --> 00:46:15.890
Lastly I just wanted to say

1328
00:46:15.890 --> 00:46:18.010
on the bottom of this slide and in the blue font,

1329
00:46:18.010 --> 00:46:20.980
that this video isn't look at coming back from an injury.

1330
00:46:20.980 --> 00:46:22.730
I'm not a physical therapist,

1331
